  "body": "Stacked on #4233. This PR contains the commits of #4233. Merge #4233 first; then this PR takes `git merge origin/main` and a new gate. Do not merge this PR before #4233.\n\n## What changed\n\nThis is U7 of #3663 and the UI scope of #3648. The tool library window now edits user holders and component stacks. It uses the component table and commands of #4201 and the user library of #4233.\n\n- **\"My library\" source** in the tools list (`tool_library_dialog/components.rs`):\n  - The list shows the built-in components and the user library file, by group (Holders, Adapters and extensions, Cutter bodies, Inserts, Solid tools), with a name filter.\n  - \"Show compatible parts\" shows only the parts that fit the picked part (`compatible_parents` and `compatible_children`).\n  - The buttons act on the picked row: Add to document, Copy as user component, Delete from My library.\n  - The document component table follows, with the library status and the users of each row: Edit component, Sync from library, Save to My library, Delete from document.\n- **Component editor** (`component_edit.rs`): name, insert code (ISO 1832), and the gauge length of a holder with a known built-in shape. \"Apply component\" is one undoable `EditDocumentComponent`. Each tool built from the part changes in the same undo step.\n- **User holders** (`holders.rs`, `holder_view.rs`): a built-in holder has \"Copy as user holder\". The Holders page lists the user holders of the document above the built-in holders.\n- **Component stack** in the assembly group of the Tool tab (`stack.rs`): the links with port, turn and stick-out, and the library status. \"Add component\" offers only the parts that fit. \"Apply stack\" is one `SetToolAssembly`. \"Detach to standalone tool\" clears the stack and keeps the tool.\n- **State** (`state_components.rs`): one `CommandKind::Component` variant and its handlers. \"Add to document\" is the upsert and the sync in one undo step (`begin_group` / `commit_group`). The library file writes (save, delete) have no undo, as the store law of #4233 says.\n- **App** (minimal, no file in `commands/` or `mcp/`): `camcraft_app` re-exports `component_fit`, `frame`, `insert_iso1832`, `insert_seat` and `tool_assembly::Mount`. Reason: the UI must not take a new crate dependency.\n- UI decisions for the owners to review or reverse: `docs/decisions/3898-tool-library-components.md`.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n`crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/tool_library_components.rs` (the \"Done means\" of #3648):\n- `my_library_lists_built_ins_and_the_user_file`\n- `the_compatible_filter_shows_the_bodies_that_take_an_insert`\n- `a_tool_is_assembled_from_linked_components_in_one_undo_step` (with undo and redo)\n- `an_edit_of_the_shared_insert_updates_both_tools_in_one_undo_step` (with undo and redo)\n- `a_newer_library_copy_syncs_into_the_document_and_its_tools` (with undo)\n- `a_built_in_holder_copies_as_a_user_holder_and_its_gauge_is_edited` (with undo)\n- `a_still_frame_reads_no_library_and_builds_nothing` (frame cost counter and changed input)\n\nLayout: `layout_window_my_library` in `page_layout_tool_library.rs`. The `#[test]` count of `crates/ui` goes up by 8. No snapshot PNG changes.\n\n## Gate results (head `8edfca4bd`, base `qsmits/issue/3645-component-library`)\n\n- Pinning tests: the 7 tests above and `layout_window_my_library` pass (`cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib`).\n- Quick gate, `cargo xtask gate quick --base qsmits/issue/3645-component-library`, on `8edfca4bd`: 21 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled. The steps: app build, app `lib`, app `tool_library_holders`, ui build, ui `lib` (the refit rule: 1728 tests, all pass), and 16 ui suites.\n- Strict clippy, `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`, on `8edfca4bd`: clean. The first run found `large_enum_variant` on `ComponentAction`; the second commit boxes the edit payload.\n- Light lane, `cargo xtask gate light --base qsmits/issue/3645-component-library`, on `0b08f9fe0`: 6 steps, 0 failed. The next commit only boxes one enum variant in the UI crate.\n- Example catalog suites: not run. No post and no toolpath changed.\n- Heavy step: none (P4).\n\n## What was not exercised\n\n- A turning tool stack. The lathe side of the resolver is open on #3643. A milling insert in an indexable cutter body stands in for the turning insert of #3648, as in the #3644 tests.\n- The assembly test sets the stack draft from `stack::candidates` and clicks \"Apply stack\". It does not click the items of the \"Add component\" combo box.\n- No heavy step (P4).\n\n## Remaining (why this PR says `Refs`, not `Fixes`)\n\n- #3648: \"assembling a turning tool from linked components\" needs the lathe resolver (#3643).\n- #3648: the derived read-only values in the stack (gauge length from the assembly) and a component swap in place.\n- #3898: its \"Done means\" includes the full list of #3648.\n- MCP tools for these commands: #3647 (a parallel worker).\n\nChangelog: The tool library window has a \"My library\" source with the component library, a compatible-parts filter and the document's component table; a component editor (name, insert code, holder gauge length) whose Apply updates every tool built from the part in one undo step; \"Copy as user holder\" on a built-in holder; and the tool's component stack on the Tool tab (Apply stack, Detach to standalone tool).\n\nEffort: high (not escalated)\n\nRefs #3898\nRefs #3648\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
